formal:
Let \(\sigma\) be the arithmetic sentence asserting that Boolean satisfiability has a deterministic polynomial-time algorithm, with the finite encodings specified below. Is \(\sigma\) independent of Zermelo–Fraenkel set theory with the axiom of choice (ZFC)? Precisely, is the following metamathematical proposition true?
\[\mathrm{ZFC}
vdash\sigma\quad	ext{and}\quad\mathrm{ZFC}
vdash
eg\sigma.\]
